PWS cpu is socketed, can be easily replaced. there is an S1 dip switch
below which sets chip operation (frequency)- it is possible to overclock
a 600MHZ chip to 667MHZ but not recommended. However any 433MHZ chip can
be replaced with a 600MHZ chip, i do this all the time. S1 settings must
be adjusted.S1 settings can be found by searching the net under 'PWS S1
settings' if i recall correctly, also Wilko on the FreeBSD list if asked
nicely can provide dip switch settings.
This CPU (contains bonded heat sink) will no fit in DS3305.
Best -Mel



