It could be the issue you're having is a common EB164 DMA bug. =20
This patch works around it.

http://skarpsey.dyndns.org/alpha-lfs/patches/linux-2.4-core_cia.patch

The issue is described at:

http://skarpsey.dyndns.org/alpha-lfs/alpha.html (search for=20
"EB164")

In any case the patch should be harmless to apply, even if it=20
doesn't fix your problem.  I've got it applied even though I=20
don't suffer from this issue.

> Is it possible that i have problems beacuse i use AlphaBios
> and not SRM?

Possibly, but IIRC AlphaBIOS+MILO should be able to handle that=20
kernel.  It's usually preferable to switch to SRM anyways, of=20
course...

--=20
