Do not use modules for scsi devices required to boot: 
hard wire this support with (Y) in kernel config file.
I had the same'panic...' message until i did just that.
FWIW you do not need anthing more than SRM consle to boot new kernel:
for me on this DS10, with dka200 as the scsi device:
>>>boot dka200 -fi 2/vmlinuz-2.4.20 -fl root=/dev/sda2 where
sda2 is /.
-Mel





